  "verbalization": "The compound {(2S)-1-[N-(tert-butoxycarbonyl)glycyl]pyrrolidin-2-yl}methyl (3-chlorophenyl)acetate is implicated in the regulation of Ig alpha-2 chain C region through multiple indirect pathways. It is predicted to act as a target for Ephrin type-A receptor 7, which in turn is a target of Phloxine B. This suggests a potential role in modulating the immune response, as Ephrin type-A receptors are involved in cell adhesion and signaling processes. Additionally, the compound is also predicted to target bacterial hemoglobin, which is a target of another compound, and this target is also linked to the Ig alpha-2 chain C region. These findings collectively suggest that the compound may influence immune-related processes through interactions with receptors and signaling molecules involved in cell adhesion and immune modulation. The evidence is supported by multiple layers of target relationships, but the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
